Recently, someone in this newsgroup mentioned that they (=the dev team) 
*might* release a "nh311-" for all those frustrated 8088 people and 286 people
who don't have enough memory to run nh3.1* properly. The "smaller" version,
he said, would have a _lot_ of features removed.

I'm just posting to see if there are any who are interested or am I alone.
I have a 286 with 1 meg ram and even after doing all the tricks in the book
(ie this newsgroup) each move still takes too much time to make the game
playable. Sounds familiar? If it does, you could post a message... maybe
if the dev team see enough us unhappy people, they'll consider releasing
a "nh311-" (or -- or ---- or -------------------- or whatever).

Is Nethack becoming an elitist hobby? The program itself is free, sure...
but definitely not everyone can afford those machines you need to run it!

